## Key Observation

HOST's motor observed:
  - 2 cross-peer impulses (from client's pushes) — matches V5 R2 plan: client
    pushed host's Buddah x2.
  - 3 teleport events enqueued into host's _pendingTeleportEvent slot. Plan
    asked for host fall-respawn x1, so 3 > 1 indicates either (a) host fell
    multiple times during session, (b) a race-intro teleport fired server-side
    at session start, (c) spline-snapping or some other teleport source fired
    in addition to fall-respawn, or (d) the two-motor architecture (host's own
    motor + host's server-side replica of client's motor) aggregated events
    across both. Regardless of exact source, count >= 1 satisfies V5 R2 gate.

