## Diagnosis for Client-side tel-compared=0 (cross-referencing host data)

User confirmed client fall-respawn fired visually during the V5 R2 session.
Host tel-compared=3 confirms host's predictionRespawnBridge is wired and
functional (respawn events enter host's queue). If the same Buddah prefab is
used for both peers (standard Unity instantiation), predictionRespawnBridge
is wired on both prefab instances.

Therefore client's tel-compared=0 with confirmed visual respawn points to
one of the BuddahRespawn.cs:156 gate conditions failing on CLIENT's instance
at call time, even though the component wiring is present:

  (a) `predictionBootstrap.IsPredictionModeActive()` — returns false on client
      when respawn fires. BUT: client's imp-compared=2 proves the same
      bootstrap returned TRUE for impulse routing in the same session. So
      either the respawn fires at a moment when the bootstrap has
      transiently flipped to Legacy, OR a different bootstrap instance is
      being checked.
  (b) `predictionRespawnBridge != null` — the bridge is present on host's
      prefab (tel-compared=3 proves). Awake() at BuddahRespawn.cs:43-45 auto-
      creates the bridge if missing. Shouldn't be null at runtime. But if
      `ResolveReferences()` inside TeleportToTrackProgress was not called
      yet when the early gate runs, or if the serialized field is null AND
      Awake hasn't resolved it yet, the check could fail transiently.
  (c) Bridge routing internally returns false on client — see
      `TryRespawnToTrackProgress` at BuddahPredictionRespawnBridge.cs:26.
      That calls `predictedMotor.RequestAuthoritativeTeleportFromOwner`
      (motor.cs:886). If motor is client-side (IsServerInitialized=false),
      it fires `RequestTeleportServerRpc` to server. If the ServerRpc
      requires ownership (RequireOwnership=true on the ServerRpc attribute),
      client must own the Buddah — which it does. Need to verify the actual
      ServerRpc signature and whether it enqueues server-side.
  (d) Client's respawn took the LEGACY path (TeleportToWorldPose at line 168)
      because the primary path's gate returned false. Visual teleport
      happens either way (rb.position = targetPosition), so user sees the
      respawn — but it never goes through the predicted queue.

Most likely (c) — the client-owner path needs the ServerRpc hop, which has
more failure modes than host's in-server direct enqueue. A code-trace of
BuddahPredictedMotor.RequestAuthoritativeTeleportFromOwner (motor.cs:886)
and RequestTeleportServerRpc (motor.cs:974) is the next diagnostic step.

## Next Step

Per user direction: await follow-up. Options on the table:
